{'symbol': 'WY', 'date': '2022-12-06 13:30:00', 'title': 'WEYERHAEUSER, AMERICAN FORESTS PARTNER TO BRING TREE EQUITY PROGRAM TO SMALLER, MORE RURAL COMMUNITIES', 'text': "STUDENTS IN THREE PILOT COMMUNITIES TO EXPLORE FORESTRY CAREERS AND SOCIAL EQUITY THROUGH DATA AND HANDS-ON PROJECTS\xa0 SEATTLE , DEC. 6, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- WEYERHAEUSER COMPANY \xa0(NYSE: WY) AND AMERICAN FORESTS , THE NATION'S OLDEST NATIONAL NONPROFIT CONSERVATION ORGANIZATION, TODAY ANNOUNCED A NEW PARTNERSHIP ON AN INNOVATIVE INITIATIVE TO EXPAND AMERICAN FORESTS' TREE EQUITY PROGRAM INTO SMALLER, MORE RURAL COMMUNITIES AND PROVIDE ENVIRONMENTAL EDUCATION FOCUSED ON CAREERS IN URBAN AND COMMUNITY FORESTRY TO HUNDREDS OF YOUTH.\u202fTHE PROGRAM AIMS TO IDENTIFY AND TACKLE DISPARITIES IN TREE CANOPY COVER IN THREE COMMUNITIES WHERE WEYERHAEUSER EMPLOYEES LIVE AND WORK AND PROVIDE REPLICABLE BEST PRACTICES FOR COMMUNITIES NATIONWIDE."}